      <title>Why the Villa Vie Odyssey Cruise Ran Out of Money for Fuel</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-11-01/why-the-villa-vie-odyssey-cruise-ran-out-of-money-for-fuel</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">f0105889f738b9c31d00110c</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 18:01:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>The saga of the Villa Vie Odyssey feels like the perfect metaphor for 2026: A year when the AI rich dreamed of a world beyond nation-states and ordinary constraints, only to run aground on the brutal reality of scarce oil. The cruise ship, on an open-ended voyage promising residents “the freedom of world travel with the comforts of home,” is stranded in Cambodia after saying it ran out of money for fuel.</description>
      <dc:creator>David Fickling</dc:creator>
